# Rangefind

> Rangefind is a static search engine: it packs a corpus into an index of plain immutable files, and the browser (or Node, or an MCP agent) answers queries by reading only the byte ranges it needs over HTTP. Full-text BM25F relevance, typo correction, facets, autocomplete, geo search, and vector/hybrid semantic search — with no search server, no SaaS, and no per-query cost.

Key facts: MIT licensed; zero runtime dependencies in the core npm package (`rangefind`); indexes proven at 7.2M-page (English Wikipedia) and 33M-place (OpenStreetMap) scale; geographic sharding federates planet-scale corpora with rankings identical to a monolithic build; every claim on this site is backed by committed, rerunnable benchmarks.

Install: `npm install rangefind`. Index a built site: `npx rangefind build ./dist`. Query from a browser via `createSearch({ baseUrl })`, from Node via `rangefind/node`, from a shell via `rangefind search`, or from an agent via the `rangefind-mcp` MCP server.

